WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.802
Let’s inspect a few values with Python’s type function.

00:00:03.802 --> 00:00:07.757
Age is thirty, so Python sees an integer.

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:11.777
Height is five point nine, so that is a float.

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:15.622
Jordan is text, so the type is string.

00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:20.893
True is a Boolean. Run the cell and verify those four results.

00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:24.270
Then put quotation marks around thirty.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:30.175
To us it still looks like the number thirty, but Python now sees text.

00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:34.765
That small change can affect whether arithmetic works correctly.

00:00:34.765 --> 00:00:41.375
Checking types is one of the simplest ways to diagnose confusing behavior in a data workflow.
